0%">36  Capital Management</span></div><div style="margin-bottom:10pt"><table style="border-collapse:collapse;display:inline-table;margin-bottom:5pt;vertical-align:text-bottom;width:100.000%"><tr><td style="width:1.0%"/><td style="width:98.900%"/><td style="width:0.1%"/></tr><tr style="height:3pt"><td colspan="3" style="border-bottom:1pt solid #0086dd;padding:0 1pt"/></tr></table></div><div style="margin-bottom:10pt"><span id="i7ed634b557b14c8cab457210cc045cec"></span><span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Calibri',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:700;line-height:120%">(i)&#160;&#160;&#160;&#160;Minimum capital requirements</span></div><div style="margin-bottom:10pt;text-align:justify"><span id="i333ed2a6000646ee8d6c6bdd41e71b55"></span><span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Calibri',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%">Although capital is managed considering the consolidated position, certain subsidiaries are subject to minimum capital requirement from local regulators.</span></div><div style="margin-bottom:10pt;text-align:justify"><span id="ibe42e921311c42c18c4e22b362e66296"></span><span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Calibri',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%">The subsidiary Banco XP, leader of the Prudential Conglomerate (which includes XP CCTVM, XP DTVM, XP Servi&#231;os Financeiros DTVM and some proprietary funds), under BACEN regulation regime, is required to maintain a minimum capital and follow aspects from the Basel Accord.</span></div><div style="margin-bottom:10pt;text-align:justify"><span id="i9e41b1b6a8ca4cc7bda297be09798264"></span><span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Calibri',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%">The subsidiary XP Vida e Previd&#234;ncia operates in retirement plans business and is oversight by the SUSEP, being required to present Adjusted Shareholders' Equity (PLA) equal to or greater than the Minimum Required Capital (&#8220;CMR&#8221;), CMR is equiv